Why Moodle Was Used

Moodle was selected as an additional knowledge source for CIHE SmartAssist because it is an important platform where students access their course-related learning materials and academic resources.

The original SmartAssist system mainly retrieves information from static CIHE documents. However, student information is not always contained in a single handbook or PDF. Moodle can contain course-specific resources such as lecture materials, pages, files, assignments, announcements, links, and other learning content.

By integrating Moodle into SmartAssist, the system can retrieve relevant information from a structured learning environment rather than depending only on manually collected documents.

Benefits of Moodle Integration

* Centralised learning information: Moodle provides a structured location for course-related resources.
* Improved information coverage: SmartAssist can access information that may not be available in the student handbook or other static documents.
* Course-specific responses: Moodle content can provide more relevant information depending on the student’s course or subject.
* Reduced manual document management: Instead of manually collecting and updating every document, Moodle content can be loaded into the SmartAssist knowledge base.
* Better RAG performance: Moodle content can be processed, embedded, and retrieved using the existing Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) pipeline.
* More realistic student support: Since students already use Moodle for their studies, integrating its resources makes SmartAssist more closely connected to their existing academic environment.

Role in CIHE SmartAssist

The Moodle integration acts as an additional data source for the RAG system. Moodle resources can be collected and processed into searchable content. When a student asks a question, SmartAssist can retrieve relevant information from both CIHE documents and Moodle resources before generating an answer.

This approach helps make the assistant more comprehensive while maintaining the project’s principle of providing answers based on available academic sources rather than allowing the AI to guess.

Future Potential

Moodle integration could later be extended to support automatic synchronisation of course materials, subject-specific information, announcements, and other authorised Moodle resources. This would allow the SmartAssist knowledge base to stay more up to date as Moodle content changes.
